    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0875" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Greece/5–1647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mark F. Ethridge to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-16T09:00:00+01:00">May 16, 1947—9 a.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>339. Ethridge 74. [Here follow two paragraphs dealing with a document presented
                    by the French, Belgian and Colombian Representatives on the Commission of
                    Investigation, which they would insert into the Commission’s report instead of
                    conclusions.]</p>
                <pb facs="0876" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>
                <p>I argued that this Commission was instructed to give SC benefit of its
                    conclusions and that SC could on the basis of conclusions reach a determination
                    if an act of aggression has been committed. Without conclusions I said there
                    would be no possibility of SC making such a determination. Another argument
                    which I used was that even if Russians veto permanent commission in SC without
                    conclusions, world public opinion would not be informed at all upon what is
                    going on in Balkans and Russia would have won great victory.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d598-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>[Here follows a further paragraph of comment and a summary of the document.]</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ethridge</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d598-f1" n="1" xml:id="d598-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 417, May 18, to Mr. Ethridge at Geneva, the Department expressed its
                    agreement “generally with position taken by you in paragraph 3 urtel 74, May
                    16.” (501.BC Greece/5–1847)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
